Goodix GM168 Linux driver provenance
====================================

This repository contains an experimental libfprint driver for USB device
27c6:589a. The implementation is licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Upstream base
-------------
libfprint v1.94.100, commit 80a4b5ec612892c5c056c48dddaa561452cf37ec
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libfprint/libfprint

Driver lineage
--------------
The current driver is a direct, substantially modified descendant of:
https://github.com/mrcook1e-ai/goodix-gm168
commit 7f7e3710bd6405b6bc238cf85fecb74e61b4d0da

That repository supplied the initial GM168 USB protocol, TLS-PSK transport,
asynchronous libfprint state machines, image-processing pipeline, and build
integration. Several protocol/support files remain verbatim or near-verbatim;
the core state machines and TLS implementation were subsequently extended and
hardened. Credit is due to repository owner mrcook1e-ai (Oleg), contributor
wseng, and the AI co-authorship disclosed in that repository's commit history.

Parts of the Goodix transport/TLS implementation derive from the
55b4-experimental libfprint work by Alexander Meiler, Matthieu Charette,
and Alireza S.N., also licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

The 27c6:589a protocol and image-processing path were independently studied
from USB traffic and behavior of the lawfully installed Windows driver. No
Goodix or Microsoft executable, firmware, VM image, private key, per-device
calibration file, biometric sample, or packet capture is distributed here.

Subsequent 27c6:589a hardware validation and fixes were performed by Daniil
Yakoshinov in 2026.
